# f1 = words
# Three loops over texts by charCodeAt, the position counted in 64 bits in the first (`at++` stands twice in its turn, and its turns are laid out): narrow and wide texts, ropes and windows of ropes, texts that end in the
# middle of a row of eight; positions that begin at, behind and far behind the end, below nothing, at a half, at 2^31, at 2^32 + 1 and at NaN; a walk backwards: 612 answers, held by a sum over their texts and by 24 written out.
